[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4844490736","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-4844490736","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":4844490736,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIMEP8A","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-30T14:20:53Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T14:20:53Z","body":"> Note that this PR does not affect left/top/right/bottom neighbor determination when navigating with the arrow keys or d-pad. It's still broken out of the box on the Drag and Drop demo:\r\n\r\n@Calinou that's strange, it should be the exact opposite. This PR handles left/top/right/bottom neighbor determination. It only didn't touch next/previous determination.\r\n\r\nI'm testing the drag&drop demo, and you're right, something strange is happening, because when a candidate fails to be found, it seems to fallback to some other logic which selects a different node. Switching to the GDScript version of the algorithm works as expected, because it completely bypasses Godot's auto focus mechanism. There's probably some behavior running elsewhere which I didn't account for, will need to find it.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7107eed1-bb08-4d0a-893c-b92a0c735e26\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4844490736/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4847879121","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-4847879121","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":4847879121,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIPTD0Q","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-30T21:01:22Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T21:01:22Z","body":"Found the issue; I forgot to discard any result returning the `NO_SCORE` constant. The drag&drop scene now works as I'd expect (I've updated the web build with the fix and this scene too).\r\n\r\nI also changed the `NO_SCORE` constant from `1e14` to `1e10`, as that can be represented in a float without precision loss and allows to test for inequality.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4847879121/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4966444000","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-4966444000","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":4966444000,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKAXr4A","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T07:24:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T07:24:47Z","body":"I've researched/tested more the `ScrollContainer` specific code, and the behavior LGTM like it is now (will update the web build demo with an example later today). As the remaining personal points are minor, I've moved the PR out of draft state.\r\n\r\nI've also forgot to do some benchmarks of this algorithm in comparison to the older one. I'll provide some results for analyis as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4966444000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4973967981","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-4973967981","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":4973967981,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKHi6bQ","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T21:02:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T21:02:42Z","body":"> Overall, it's better in Balloon but there is still one case where it unexpectedly goes to the left column's CheckButton while pressing Down (while the HSlider in the middle column is focused).\r\n\r\nHere's the visualization of the candidates in that scenario:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1632\" height=\"896\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1701b312-e28c-4cf4-8139-362e4dff1df9\" />\r\n\r\nFrom an algorithm point of view, it makes sense, but indeed the visual interpretation feels wrong. With that said, these cases will always be subjective IMO. Here's a similar scenario with less visual clutter. Now this behavior now feels more logical to me than the previous scenario, even though they are objectively the same:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"940\" height=\"517\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/22efc339-aecb-43a8-8712-94d00681070b\" />\r\n\r\nThis is to say that, although there's of course room for future improvement (I recall the original discussion at some point prioritizing circle expansion in the input direction; sorta like having growing ovals instead of circles), the algorithm will never be infallible.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4973967981/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4974102117","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-4974102117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":4974102117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKHrGZQ","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T21:20:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T21:20:21Z","body":"I've updated the web build with new demo scenes. I didn't get the chance to explore benchmarks for today, hopefully tomorrow I can have a got at it :relieved: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4974102117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4995285176","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-4995285176","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":4995285176,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKb4AuA","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T18:28:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T18:29:12Z","body":"> In particular, I'm thinking about a variation of the balloon algorithm that is less '4-directional' and more 'any direction' – and thus potentially more intuitive with joystick controls or UI's that desire diagonal navigation\r\n\r\nThis is actually already supported by this algorithm, and even on the legacy one, as both variants take in an arbitrary input `Vector2`. This 4-directional limitation is coming from Godot itself, not from the algorithms.\r\n\r\nDuring development, I've patched the engine out of curiosity to check how it fares, and the balloon algorithm works perfectly with 360° joystick input on complex scenes, such as the skill tree one (I didn't test the legacy one back then, but in theory it is also supported).\r\n\r\nBut, the reason why I didn't already include this improvement in this PR is because it isn't straightforward yet to support this input range in UI nodes; during my tests, Godot constantly switched between two directions on a diagonal input, leading to dozens of node focus being changed in less than a second. This is due to the analog nature of the joystick, and the movement constantly generating UP/DOWN/RIGHT/LEFT events at the slightest value change.\r\n\r\nIt's definitely an awesome future improvement which will make this algorithm even more reliable. But there's more work to be done in the engine to fully support this, so I think it's best to leave it for a future PR/proposal.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4995285176/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5078203210","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5078203210","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5078203210,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLq87Sg","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-25T10:47:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-25T10:47:16Z","body":"Finally got some time to experiment with a rough benchmark of these algorithms. I've tested this under a scene with 10k button nodes, all scattered randomly. Then tested frame time spent on 5 input events through Tracy:\r\n<img width=\"1625\" height=\"853\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/982c7e66-c359-400f-93ed-235adcad00cb\" />\r\n\r\nHere are the observed times and their average:\r\n||Legacy algorithm|Balloon algorithm|\r\n|-|-|-|\r\n|Times (`_input` function)|172.17ms|176.01ms|\r\n||169.97ms|174.94ms|\r\n||169.12ms|178.67ms|\r\n||175.52ms|180.07ms|\r\n||179.12ms|178.38ms|\r\n|**Average**|**173.18ms**|**177.614ms**|\r\n|**Delta**| _baseline_ | **+4.434ms (+2.56%)** |\r\n\r\nEven though there's a measured performance impact, I find it pretty negligible (especially considering this specific scenario of 10k Control nodes seems very unlikely to exist on real projects).\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5078203210/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":9,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5166675181","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5166675181","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5166675181,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM_U07Q","user":{"login":"francoisdlt","id":935800,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzNTgwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/935800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt","html_url":"https://github.com/francoisdlt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-03T13:06:12Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T13:06:12Z","body":"tested on a small sample project and the new algorithm is much better","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5166675181/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433133972","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5433133972","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5433133972,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ9cLlA","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T01:20:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T01:20:25Z","body":"I just tested the latest build from the CI, and it appears this case is not correct? The first button in a vbox is selected, then down is pressed, and the middle button is skipped, the bottom one gets focused.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/47e4c6ae-8a89-441e-ac55-9d5c79f75f46\r\n\r\nProject:\r\n[balloon_algo_test_2026-08-26_21-16-52.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31494324/balloon_algo_test_2026-08-26_21-16-52.zip)\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433133972/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5436050719","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5436050719","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5436050719,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRAONHw","user":{"login":"runevision","id":6685642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2ODU2NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6685642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision","html_url":"https://github.com/runevision","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T07:51:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T07:51:38Z","body":"> The first button in a vbox is selected, then down is pressed, and the middle button is skipped, the bottom one gets focused.\r\n\r\nI assume the buttons are slightly overlapping?\r\n\r\nI warned at some point a while back than the current chosen implementation does not behave well with overlapping elements. But not being directly involved, I didn't want to repeat it if everyone actually involved seemed happy.\r\n\r\nUnlike Unity's implementation, this one tests from one control edge to another, which has a number of advantages, but fails at handling overlaps. To avoid this issue, some kind of shrinking of control bounds (probably by a user-defined amount) is needed for the purposes of the focus behavior. Of course, I don't mean that the bounds should be shrunk in general; e.g. they shouldn't affect layout and hit testing etc.\r\n\r\nThe shrinking could be an inset from all sides (e.g., width is shrunk 8 pixels, height is shrunk 8 pixels), which is what I'd recommend. Alternatively, a percentage (e.g., width is shrunk 10%, height is shrunk 10%).","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5436050719/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5436115596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5436115596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5436115596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRASKjA","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T07:58:10Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T07:58:10Z","body":"@runevision this is what I assumed initially as well, but there is indeed a bug here; beyond replicating @Goldenlion5648's case, I also cannot move towards any left control anymore.\r\n\r\nMy latest changes are probably the issue as I did a small refactor. I'll double check the math and hopefully the solution also solves the reported case. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5436115596/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5453329986","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5453329986","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5453329986,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRQs2Qg","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T13:50:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T13:50:02Z","body":"The issue was actually a good ol' `NaN` comparison bug. I had changed the comparison order between current and candidate score, which is usually fine, except when `NaN`'s are involved :upside_down_face: .\r\n\r\nI've added an extra check when fetching the line to line intersection to see if it actually intersects, which should prevent such cases from now on. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5453329986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5479607001","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5479607001","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5479607001,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRpwq2Q","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"U