ey cycles through all, at the end of the clip\r\n\r\n[Screencast_20260901_013507.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6fd55e79-5e8e-4ac9-b902-db8a2dbb554c)\r\n\r\nsame thing happens in the inspector when changing project setting to balloon. It skips the middle button. Legacy does not do this\r\n\r\n[Screencast_20260901_014543.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19761c40-4f56-4f1c-8506-5d7cf0a30300)\r\n\r\nAnchor preset menu also have same problem with keyboard navigation skipping buttons.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5486290106/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5489947726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5489947726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5489947726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRzn0Tg","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T06:39:41Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T06:39:41Z","body":"@Giganzo this might be the overlap issue @runevision mentioned. If this is used extensively in the editor then probably we need to explore a \"bias\" solution for this. I'll have a look at this later this week.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5489947726/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5490562782","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5490562782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5490562782,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR0NW3g","user":{"login":"Giganzo","id":158825920,"node_id":"U_kgDOCXd9wA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158825920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo","html_url":"https://github.com/Giganzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T07:37:50Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T07:37:50Z","body":"TabContainer has same problem with the popupmenu button (set_popup).\r\n\r\nLegacy:\r\n\r\n[Screencast_20260901_093552.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef337bee-38f1-4d48-a743-75e74812d5aa)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBalloon:\r\n\r\n[Screencast_20260901_093615.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1cb2230f-45ce-4543-9c55-667ab09bae4c)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5490562782/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5490951214","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5490951214","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5490951214,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR0lELg","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T08:11:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T08:11:00Z","body":"As the starting point is the center of the edge of the bounding box, perhaps it can be one pixel to the center center of the bounding box? or even a configurable amount / ratio? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5490951214/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5491119692","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120631#issuecomment-5491119692","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120631","id":5491119692,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR0vWTA","user":{"login":"runevision","id":6685642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2ODU2NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6685642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision","html_url":"https://github.com/runevision","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runevision/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T08:24:47Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T08:24:47Z","body":"> As the starting point is the center of the edge of the bounding box, perhaps it can be one pixel to the center center of the bounding box? or even a configurable amount / ratio?\r\n\r\nI would recommend solutions that don't assume the current 4-directional limitation and will also work for any-directional thumbstick input in the future.\r\n\r\nLike I said before, shrinking the considered rects being evaluated would be the simplest solution. (Not by changing the existing rects but by comparing with a shrunken copy, purely mathematically.) I global amount would probably suffice (but not shared between the editor and game of course). Perhaps Godot has some context for UI where it could reside (forgive my limited Godot knowledge here). Having it on every single GUI element would be overkill IMO and make it harder to test changing it.\r\n\r\nA sensible default could be 1 pixel, so rects are shrunk by one pixel on each edge. The rect width is shrunk by 2 pixels (1 for left edge and 1 for right edge) and the rect height is shrunk by 2 pixels (one for top edge and one for bottom edge). This should avoid all issues caused by touching UI elements and floating point precision limitations, while having minimal impact on behavior.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5491119692/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]